{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Repaired the billing migration package:\n\n- Updated `billingdb/migration.sql`\n  - Explicit transactional migration.\n  - Preserves invoices, payments, and historical `created_at`.\n  - Adds `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'`.\n  - Moves orphan `p4` into `payment_orphans`.\n  - Rebuilds `payments` with a foreign key to `invoices`.\n  - Supports safe repeated execution without duplicating rows or resetting changed statuses.\n  - Restores `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON`.\n\n- Added `billingdb/preflight_report.md`\n  - Documents source counts and orphan `p4`.\n\n- Added `billingdb/postcheck.sql`\n  - Checks counts, orphan preservation, statuses, invalid references, FK violations, and FK definition.\n\n- Added `billingdb/rollback.sql`\n  - Restores the original table shapes.\n  - Restores preserved orphan payments to the legacy `payments` table.\n  - Removes migration bookkeeping.\n\n- Added `billingdb/migration_report.md`\n  - Documents safety behavior, idempotence, rollback semantics, and postchecks.\n\nVerification completed using SQLite:\n\n- Clean migration postcheck: all checks passed.\n- Second migration run: counts remained `(invoices=3, payments=3, orphans=1)`.\n- Modified invoice status survived rerun.\n- Rollback restored columns:\n  - `invoices(id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at)`\n  - `payments(id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at)`\n- Rollback restored all four payments, including `p4`."}}
